{"title":"Career Roadmap · Pathology Lab Technician","role":"Pathology Lab Technician","summary":"A Pathology Lab Technician performs and supports laboratory investigations used for disease diagnosis, monitoring, screening, and treatment decisions.","facts":{"Current degree":"BMLT / B.Sc Medical Laboratory Technology","Course":"Medical Laboratory Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Pathology Lab Technician performs and supports laboratory investigations used for disease diagnosis, monitoring, screening, and treatment decisions."},{"type":"p","text":"The role involves handling patient specimens and performing laboratory procedures across areas such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical biochemistry"},{"text":"Hematology"},{"text":"Clinical pathology"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Histopathology"},{"text":"Immunology"},{"text":"Serology"},{"text":"Blood banking/transfusion services"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong laboratory professional must prioritize specimen integrity, analytical accuracy, biosafety, quality control, documentation, and result reliability."},{"type":"p","text":"The career is particularly suitable for students who prefer laboratory science, diagnostic technology and analytical work over direct bedside patient care."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2028"},{"text":"Laboratory fundamentals, specimen handling and biosafety"}],[{"text":"2028–2030"},{"text":"Hematology, biochemistry, microbiology and clinical pathology"}],[{"text":"2030–2032"},{"text":"Independent laboratory operations and quality systems"}],[{"text":"2032–2035"},{"text":"Senior Lab Technician / Technologist"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Specialized laboratory technology / supervisory roles"}],[{"text":"2040+"},{"text":"Laboratory management, quality or technical leadership"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Exact professional titles, scope of practice and registration requirements should be checked against applicable state/national regulations and employer requirements."}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Laboratory Science Foundation","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build a strong scientific foundation."},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anatomy"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Pathology fundamentals"},{"text":"Basic hematology"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Laboratory mathematics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Laboratory fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Laboratory safety"},{"text":"PPE"},{"text":"Sterilization"},{"text":"Disinfection"},{"text":"Glassware handling"},{"text":"Pipetting"},{"text":"Centrifugation"},{"text":"Sample labeling"},{"text":"Basic microscopy"},{"text":"Laboratory documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specimen awareness"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand correct handling of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Blood"},{"text":"Urine"},{"text":"Stool"},{"text":"Sputum"},{"text":"Swabs"},{"text":"Body fluids"},{"text":"Tissue specimens"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Core Medical Laboratory Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop practical laboratory competence."},{"type":"h","text":"Hematology"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hemoglobin"},{"text":"RBC parameters"},{"text":"WBC count"},{"text":"Differential count"},{"text":"Platelets"},{"text":"ESR"},{"text":"Peripheral blood smear"},{"text":"Basic coagulation testing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the clinical relevance of common abnormalities."},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical biochemistry"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn principles behind:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Blood glucose"},{"text":"Liver function tests"},{"text":"Kidney function tests"},{"text":"Lipid profile"},{"text":"Electrolytes"},{"text":"Enzymes"},{"text":"Proteins"},{"text":"Bilirubin"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical pathology"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop skills in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Urinalysis"},{"text":"Stool examination"},{"text":"Body-fluid examination"},{"text":"Routine microscopy"},{"text":"Physical and chemical analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Microbiology, Immunology & Advanced Diagnostics"},{"type":"h","text":"Microbiology"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bacteriology"},{"text":"Virology fundamentals"},{"text":"Mycology"},{"text":"Parasitology"},{"text":"Culture techniques"},{"text":"Staining techniques"},{"text":"Antibiotic susceptibility testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important techniques"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gram staining"},{"text":"Acid-fast staining"},{"text":"Culture"},{"text":"Microscopy"},{"text":"Colony identification"},{"text":"Basic antimicrobial susceptibility testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Immunology & serology"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Antigen-antibody reactions"},{"text":"ELISA principles"},{"text":"Rapid diagnostic tests"},{"text":"Immunoassays"},{"text":"Serological testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 / Final Clinical Training — Diagnostic Laboratory Practice"},{"type":"p","text":"The final phase should integrate laboratory science with real clinical workflow."},{"type":"h","text":"Histopathology exposure"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn fundamentals of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tissue processing"},{"text":"Fixation"},{"text":"Dehydration"},{"text":"Embedding"},{"text":"Sectioning"},{"text":"Staining"},{"text":"Slide preparation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the role of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Formalin fixation"},{"text":"Paraffin embedding"},{"text":"Microtomy"},{"text":"H&E staining"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cytology awareness"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop basic understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cytology specimens"},{"text":"Smear preparation"},{"text":"Staining"},{"text":"Screening principles"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Blood banking"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ABO grouping"},{"text":"Rh typing"},{"text":"Crossmatching"},{"text":"Blood-component basics"},{"text":"Transfusion safety"},{"text":"Storage principles"}]}]},{"heading":"Specimen Management","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Specimen quality directly affects diagnostic accuracy."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn the complete workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Identification","Correct Specimen Collection","Correct Labeling","Transport","Reception","Processing","Analysis","Quality Check","Result Validation","Reporting","Record Retention"]},{"type":"h","text":"Common pre-analytical errors"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand risks from:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Wrong patient identification"},{"text":"Incorrect container"},{"text":"Insufficient sample"},{"text":"Hemolysis"},{"text":"Improper storage"},{"text":"Delayed transport"},{"text":"Incorrect labeling"},{"text":"Contamination"}]}]},{"heading":"Laboratory Quality Management","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A good technician is not simply someone who can operate instruments."},{"type":"p","text":"They must understand quality assurance and quality control."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Internal Quality Control"},{"text":"External Quality Assessment"},{"text":"Calibration"},{"text":"Reference ranges"},{"text":"Control materials"},{"text":"Equipment maintenance"},{"text":"Method validation concepts"},{"text":"Quality indicators"},{"text":"Non-conformance management"},{"text":"Corrective actions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Quality workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sample","Correct Method","QC Check","Analysis","Result Verification","Reporting","Quality Monitoring"]}]},{"heading":"Biosafety","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Biosafety sho